                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96ac27a3-31fa-36ae-be19-440d872f4954",
                        "entry_id": "18b007d5-9877-35bf-af4c-7d06e77bc8b9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "o zwierzęciu: mający umaszczenie o ciemnych pasach na jaśniejszym tle"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08bafc4e-e22a-4150-8ed7-11877d87afc4",
                        "source_entry_id": "18b007d5-9877-35bf-af4c-7d06e77bc8b9",
                        "source_sense_id": "96ac27a3-31fa-36ae-be19-440d872f4954",
                        "target_lang_word": "brindled",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brindled",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f65f582b-593b-3bda-862f-917b8b06f91e",
                                        "entry_id": "f1fc1a5d-05f2-3888-9006-91d944c4dd5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a brownish, tawny or gray colour, with streaks or spots; streaky, spotted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7f683dc-fb38-4fa2-acc9-e3d07a6bcfe7",
                                                "sense_id": "f65f582b-593b-3bda-862f-917b8b06f91e",
                                                "text": "The palace in a woody vale they found,\nHigh raised of stone; a shaded space around;\nWhere mountain wolves and brindled lions roam,\n(By magic tamed,) familiar to the dome."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b88547c-9d2e-4e2c-93f2-cfebd1a8c706",
                                                "sense_id": "f65f582b-593b-3bda-862f-917b8b06f91e",
                                                "text": "All round me were tokens of a divided empire. The old grass and the new grass were striving together. In the low wet swales the verdure peeped out in vivid green ; beyond, on the mountains, lay light patches of snow, strangely relieved against their russet sides; all the humped hills looked like brindled kine in the shivers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9f1fb21-d6e5-45ec-b64f-e9434c4659cb",
                                                "sense_id": "f65f582b-593b-3bda-862f-917b8b06f91e",
                                                "text": "And there, in the middle of it was the man himself—his face twisted like a lost soul in torment, and his great brindled beard stuck upwards in his agony."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed966c8e-9f77-4795-8b18-303b3fc7febb",
                                                "sense_id": "f65f582b-593b-3bda-862f-917b8b06f91e",
                                                "text": "Some brindled curs hurried from beneath the houses to sniff at Flo […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "brindled",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d9feea8-28ff-3b6b-8498-de32652bb9b6",
                                        "entry_id": "bbf16563-19a7-3f8b-a56d-8ad052b69cd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of brindle"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64da6879-0833-4906-9c96-1939889aaa48",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9feea8-28ff-3b6b-8498-de32652bb9b6",
                                                "text": "Apples, these I mean, unspeakably fair [...] - some brindled with deep red streaks like a cow, or with hundreds of fine blood-red rays running regularly from the stem-dimple to the blossom-end, like meridional lines, on a straw-colored ground, [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e43c7335-b2b3-4d8d-8207-2ca13c4f13b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "18b007d5-9877-35bf-af4c-7d06e77bc8b9",
                        "source_sense_id": "96ac27a3-31fa-36ae-be19-440d872f4954",
                        "target_lang_word": "brinded",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brinded",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d946d3bc-c11d-37c7-879d-bab3eb531891",
                                        "entry_id": "86038ab9-e334-35f0-86a2-70770c1039a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Especially of the fur or skin of animals: having a patchy or streaky pattern, usually brown or grey in colour; brindled."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "380d8100-f7a4-48b2-990d-daedbf5c8061",
                                                "sense_id": "d946d3bc-c11d-37c7-879d-bab3eb531891",
                                                "text": "Thrice the brinded Cat hath mew'd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ceca026e-7771-4b77-9c2d-0b6be16252d5",
                                                "sense_id": "d946d3bc-c11d-37c7-879d-bab3eb531891",
                                                "text": "It is well known that the only wool susceptible of acquiring delicate and brilliant colours by the process of dyeing, is white wool: for this reason the Cachemirians separate all those lambs which are black or brinded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d8199a1-194b-4f88-a895-be7432c4aee5",
                                                "sense_id": "d946d3bc-c11d-37c7-879d-bab3eb531891",
                                                "text": "Glory be to God for dappled things— / For skies of couple-colour as a brinded cow; / For rose-moles all in stipple upon trout that swim: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e3c07f7-230f-335e-9c61-af1a8dcd3f2c",
                                        "entry_id": "86038ab9-e334-35f0-86a2-70770c1039a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Frowning, looking sour or angry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c47a2e8f-a625-4bf4-a527-29256cdb81cd",
                                                "sense_id": "9e3c07f7-230f-335e-9c61-af1a8dcd3f2c",
                                                "text": "Lawks, doant be clummed by Babbin Enapp,\n'Sa bibbling, boostering, brinded chap,\n A dinderhead hadge-boar!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
